  "worked_solution": "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m\u2220A={45}^{\u2218}.$ Notice that relative to $\u2220A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{\u2015}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{\u2015}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061(m\u2220A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}\u2061({45}^{\u2218}) & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{x+3}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =x+3 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x+3=3+3=6, \\\\ AB & =2x=2(3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\u25b3ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
